                <pb facs="0245" n="153" xml:id="pg153"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr. Hay</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Pekin, China</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1899-12-09"><hi rendition="#italic">December
                                9, 1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 290.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Complying with Department’s instructions
                    No. 211 of September 19 last, I have the honor to inclose a copy of Consul
                    Johnson’s final report upon the Japanese concession at Amoy, and to say that no
                    effort is at present being made to obtain an international foreign settlement,
                    nor secure to American interests privileges equivalent to those granted to
                    Japan.</p>
                <p>The few Americans there do not need such a concession, nor could they afford the
                    expense of controlling and keeping it up.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d123-a1.xml" xpointer="d123-a1"/>
